em reliability.\\" This approach makes your accomplishments more impactful and measurable."]}, {"title": "Lead Ambassador I4G CUCG", "description": "This section highlights your leadership experience and involvement in building a developer community. While it showcases your passion for fostering tech growth, it could be further strengthened by quantifying the impact of your efforts.", "ats_match": 75, "recommendations": ["Consider adding details like the number of hackathons or events you organized, the number of participants you engaged, or the specific contributions you made to the I4G community. This will make your achievements more concrete and tangible for recruiters."]}, {"title": "Education", "description": "This section provides the essential information about your academic background. It\'s well-presented and accurately reflects your degree and institution. However, consider adding any relevant coursework or projects that highlight your technical skills or relevant industry experience.", "ats_match": 80, "recommendations": ["Add a brief description of your most relevant coursework or projects. For example, \'Developed a mobile application for X using Y technologies\' or \'Led a team project on Z, utilizing A and B.\'"]}, {"title": "Skills", "description": "You\'ve listed a strong set of technical skills, covering programming languages, frameworks, and tools. This demonstrates your technical proficiency and ability to work with various technologies. However, consider adding a brief description of your expertise in each skill to showcase your level of mastery.", "ats_match": 95, "recommendations": ["Consider adding a brief description of your skills. For example, instead of \'JavaScript,\' you could write \'JavaScript (3 years of experience, proficient in React and Node.js).\']"}]}\n'}
